Gordon, played by Gary Oldman.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The Dark Knight is a 2008 superhero film directed by Christopher Nolan,
from a screenplay co-written with his brother Jonathan.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Based on the DC Comics superhero Batman, it is the sequel to Batman Begins
(2005), and the second installment in The Dark Knight trilogy.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The plot follows the vigilante Batman, police lieutenant James Gordon, and district attorney
Harvey Dent, who form an alliance to dismantle organized crime in Gotham City.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Their efforts are derailed by the Joker, an anarchistic mastermind who seeks
to test how far Batman will go to save the city from chaos.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
The ensemble cast includes Christian Bale, Michael Caine, Heath Ledger, Gary
Oldman, Aaron Eckhart, Maggie Gyllenhaal, and Morgan Freeman.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Warner Bros.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Pictures prioritized a sequel following the successful
reinvention of the Batman film series with Batman Begins.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Christopher and Batman Begins co-writer David S.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Goyer developed the story elements, making Dent the central protagonist
caught up in the battle between Batman and the Joker.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
In writing the screenplay, the Nolans were influenced by 1980s Batman comics and crime drama
films, and sought to continue Batman Begins' heightened sense of realism.

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
From April to November 2007, filming took place with a $185 million
budget in Chicago and Hong Kong, and on sets in England.

24
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
The Dark Knight was the first major motion picture to be
filmed with high-resolution IMAX cameras.

25
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Christopher avoided using computer-generated imagery unless necessary, insisting on
practical stunts such as flipping an 18-wheel truck and blowing up a factory.

26
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
The Dark Knight was marketed with an innovative interactive viral campaign that initially focused on countering
criticism of Ledger's casting by those who believed he was a poor choice to portray the Joker.

27
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
Ledger died from an accidental prescription drug overdose in January 2008, leading to
widespread interest from the press and public regarding his performance.

28
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
When it was released in July, The Dark Knight received acclaim for its mature tone and themes, visual style, and performances—particularly that of Ledger, who received many posthumous
awards including Academy, BAFTA, and Golden Globe awards for Best Supporting Actor, making The Dark Knight the first comic-book film to receive major acting awards.

29
01:56:00,000 --> 01:56:06,000
It broke several box-office records and became the highest-grossing 2008 film, the
fourth-highest-grossing film to that time, and the highest-grossing superhero film of the time.

30
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
Since its release, The Dark Knight has been assessed as one of the greatest superhero films
ever, one of the best movies of the 2000s, and one of the best films ever made.

31
02:04:00,000 --> 02:04:06,000
It is considered the "blueprint" for many modern superhero films, particularly for its rejection of a
typical comic-book movie style in favor of a crime film that features comic-book characters.

32
02:08:00,000 --> 02:08:06,000
Many filmmakers attempted to replicate its success by adopting a
similarly gritty, realistic tone, though with uneven results.

33
02:12:00,000 --> 02:12:06,000
The Dark Knight has been analyzed for its themes of terrorism
and the limitations of morality and ethics.

34
02:16:00,000 --> 02:16:06,000
The United States Library of Congress selected it for
preservation in the National Film Registry in 2020.

35
02:20:00,000 --> 02:20:06,000
A sequel, The Dark Knight Rises, concluded The Dark Knight trilogy in 2012.

36
02:24:00,000 --> 02:24:06,000
The film explores themes of sadism, chaos, secret
identity, crime fighter, superhero.

37
02:28:00,000 --> 02:28:06,000
The tone is dark and intense.
